// ═══ ClassNotFoundException — dynamic loading fails ═══
try {
    // Load JDBC driver by name — string-based, dynamic:
    Class.forName("com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver");  // driver JAR not on classpath!
} catch (ClassNotFoundException e) {
    // CHECKED exception — compiler forces handling!
    // CAUSE: typo in class name, missing JAR, wrong classpath
    log.error("MySQL driver not found — add mysql-connector-j to pom.xml!", e);
}

// Class.forName("com.bank.SomePlugin")  → ClassNotFoundException if plugin JAR missing
// ClassLoader.loadClass("com.vendor.X")  → ClassNotFoundException if vendor JAR missing
// These are DYNAMIC lookups — the class name is a STRING. Compiler can't verify it exists.

// ═══ NoClassDefFoundError — was there at compile, gone at runtime ═══
// Code compiled with: import com.vendor.PaymentGateway;
public class PaymentService {
    public void pay() {
        PaymentGateway gateway = new PaymentGateway();  // DIRECT reference — compiled successfully
        gateway.process();
    }
}
// At compile time: PaymentGateway.class WAS on classpath → code compiled.
// At runtime: vendor.jar NOT deployed → JVM can't find PaymentGateway.class
// → NoClassDefFoundError!
// This is an ERROR — deployment problem, not something to catch and handle.

// Another cause: static initializer failure
public class Config {
    static {
        // This runs when the class is FIRST loaded:
        int value = Integer.parseInt("NOT_A_NUMBER");  // NumberFormatException!
    }
}
// First attempt: Class.forName("Config") → ExceptionInInitializerError
// Second attempt: new Config() → NoClassDefFoundError!
// WHY: JVM marks the class as "failed to initialize" — won't try again.
```

Comparison:

```java
// Feature             | ClassNotFoundException          | NoClassDefFoundError
// ────────────────────|─────────────────────────────────|──────────────────────
// Type                | CHECKED Exception               | ERROR (unchecked)
// When                | Dynamic loading (Class.forName) | Direct reference at runtime
// Cause               | Class never on classpath        | Was on classpath at compile, missing at runtime
// Compile time        | No guarantee (string-based)     | GUARANTEED (direct import)
// Fix                 | Add JAR, fix class name         | Fix deployment, include dependency
// Should catch?       | YES (checked — forced)          | NO (Error — deployment problem)
```

